  "notes": "USAGE:\n- {回診|かいしん}する (to make rounds)\n- {回診|かいしん}に{来|く}る (to come on rounds)\n- {教授|きょうじゅ}{回診|かいしん} (professor's rounds - teaching hospital context)\n- {朝|あさ}の{回診|かいしん} (morning rounds)\nA standard practice in hospitals where doctors visit each patient's bedside to assess their condition. In teaching hospitals, rounds often include medical students and residents.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {往診|おうしん} (house call - visiting patients at home)\n- {診察|しんさつ} (medical examination)\n- {入院|にゅういん} (hospitalization)",
